          "x": 0,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: get-ready-with-me\nTopic: AI tools\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 12s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_YV22GYXR99W89VGGH7KJ2127FK",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_2VJ6K6E3E9B76NCF1GVZS535CF",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_GD3CXP0GMCM8J30G7X9H0MV9XJ",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.72,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a get-ready-with-me about AI tools for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the get-ready-with-me \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a top-down descent onto a flat plane on a 180mm long macro, framing with a stacked layered composition with three depth planes.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with bare-bulb specular light producing tight, hot speculars; grade as Eterna-style muted greens with gentle highlight roll-off. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. Reply with a single continuous prompt paragraph. Never explain, never bullet, never wrap it in markdown fences."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_D4TS6AWK7D8XWG1PDDCR57VEJC",
